+    """patches/0460: per component, median / p90 in microseconds over the traced ops of one rank:
+
+    - ``stage``  kernel start -> doorbell (staging copy + fences);
+    - ``wait``   doorbell -> the peer's flags seen (the peer's lateness + proxy + wire + NIC write + visibility);
+    - ``copy``   flags seen -> kernel end (copy-out + tail);
+    - ``total``  start -> end;
+    - ``notice`` doorbell (GPU globaltimer) -> the proxy saw it (CPU CLOCK_REALTIME): meaningful only if the two
+      clocks agree (on GB10 the driver keeps globaltimer on the host's clock; check that ``notice`` is small and
+      positive), ``post`` the proxy's ibv_post_send calls.
+    With ``peer_rows`` (the other rank's rows, same seqs): per op the smaller of the two ranks' waits is the
+    transport (neither rank was waiting for a late peer), the difference is the skew (``transport`` / ``skew``)."""
+
+    comp: dict[str, list] = {k: [] for k in ("stage", "wait", "copy", "total", "notice", "post")}
